 "name": "Erbil Built Heritage: Semantic Differential",
 "description": "Faithful replication of Sektani, Khayat, Mohammadi & Roders (2021), \"Erbil City Built Heritage and Wellbeing: An Assessment of Local Perceptions Using the Semantic Differential Scale\", Sustainability 13:3763. Participants give gender, age and academic attainment (architect or non-architect), then see Section A (six photographs of high-quality heritage buildings in the buffer zone of Erbil Citadel, Iraq, shown together) and Section B (six photographs of contrasting modern buildings, shown together). For each section they rate the buildings on the paper's 30 bipolar adjective pairs (qualitative, heritage-value and affective-evaluative variables) on a 5-point scale from +2 to −2, in the item order of the paper's questionnaire. Analysis as in the paper: item means and SDs per section, Mann–Whitney U tests between architects and non-architects, correlations between the three variates. Photographs: the paper's own photographs (Table 3 and the questionnaire in Appendix B, CC BY 4.0), used with credit; the template is removed if the authors object. Differences from the original study: (1) online self-completion instead of an interactive face-to-face questionnaire; (2) English only (the original form also gave Kurdish and Arabic wording); (3) age is entered as whole years from 18 and every pair must be answered before moving on; (4) the photographs are shown in a grid next to the word pairs and can be enlarged, instead of printed on the form.",
